// Title: C# IL Code Compilation Via Ilasm.EXE
// Sigma ID: 850d55f9-6eeb-4492-ad69-a72338f65ba4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-05-07 | Modified: 2026-11-21
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects the use of "Ilasm.EXE" in order to compile C# intermediate (IL) code to EXE or DLL.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Ilasm/
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20231017050336/https://www.echotrail.io/insights/search/ilasm.exe
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/9493cf5c565d7a01b8f064e01a51e1b94057e4bb/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ilasm_il_code_compilation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ilasm.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ilasm.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains " /dll" or ProcessCommandLine contains " /exe")
